WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.200
MyCampusView Academy. Robotics 101, video 14: The final challenge.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.950
You have built it, programmed it and tuned it.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.150
Now it is time to show what your robot can do.

4
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:22.029
Your challenge track has a start, some gentle curves, an S-bend, at

5
00:00:22.079 --> 00:00:28.026
least one sharp corner, and a black finish line across the track

6
00:00:28.076 --> 00:00:30.650
where the robot should stop.

7
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:37.826
Here is a full run in the simulator with pivot turns.

8
00:00:37.876 --> 00:00:44.650
Smooth, steady, and on the line all the way to the end.

9
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.595
There are three ways to hand in your project.

10
00:00:49.645 --> 00:00:55.098
If you built it, add a photo, your code and a video link.

11
00:00:55.148 --> 00:01:00.022
If your teacher watched it run, choose that option.

12
00:01:00.072 --> 00:01:07.650
If you have no kit, finish the S-curve and sharp-turns tracks in the simulator.

13
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.610
Your teacher looks at four things.

14
00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:15.069
Does it follow the line to the end?

15
00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:19.121
Does it handle the curves and the corner?

16
00:01:19.171 --> 00:01:20.999
Is your code clean?

17
00:01:21.049 --> 00:01:25.150
And can you explain one problem you fixed?

18
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:31.239
After your teacher approves it, take the final assessment to earn your

19
00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:35.082
certificate and the Line-Follower Champion badge.

20
00:01:35.132 --> 00:01:36.650
Well done, engineer!

21
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:43.500
Next: The final assessment, then your certificate.
